#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""flowd: live data-flow stream for the dashboard's Architecture map (Server-Sent Events).

Tails my session transcripts (the main session + its recently active subagents; incrementally, never loaded whole),
~/inbox and the dashboard data file, turns every step into an event on an edge of the map ("from→to") and streams it,
filtered, over SSE. nginx serves it as dash.<domain>/live (same basic auth). The container publishes no port for
it, so an ssh reverse tunnel carries it: nginx VM 127.0.0.1:PORT -> container 127.0.0.1:PORT.

  flowd serve [--port N] [--static DIR]  run the server in the foreground on 127.0.0.1 (--static: also serve DIR's
                                         index.html + data.json, for local tests and screenshots)
  flowd ensure      watchdog (cron every minute + boot.sh): start server + tunnel unless switched off; restart a hung one
  flowd off         KILL SWITCH: stop both and stay off, also across reboots  ·  flowd on: switch back on
  flowd stop        stop both (the next ensure restarts them)  ·  flowd status: processes + health
  flowd probe [P]   GET https://dash.<domain>/live/health (or P) through nginx; basic auth from ~/.secrets, never printed
                    (handle "dash": local = that curl; shadow = it + the hub's check; hub = through core.egress,
                    the hub puts the credential on the wire, no local file read)
  flowd edges       list the edge ids

HTTP (127.0.0.1:PORT; nginx location /live)
  GET /live?edge=ID[,ID][&pulse=1]  SSE. ID = "from→to" (also from-to, from>to), up to 4, "*" = all, "" = none. "hello",
                               the edge's backlog (ring of 80; Last-Event-ID resumes), then live "ev" events; pulse=1
                               adds a content-free "pulse" {edge,from,to,kind} for the other edges; ": ping" every 15 s.
       optional filters (backlog and live, to cut bandwidth): kind=K[,K] (up to 12), from=NODE, to=NODE,
       dir=in|out (to me / from me), err=1 (errors only: exit != 0, error flag or chip "error"), since=EPOCH (events
       at/after), q=TEXT (≤ 200 chars, case-insensitive, all words must match). q only ever sees what the event
       already carries (filtered text, chip, kind, actor, nodes, meta), never hidden or vault content. Bad value -> 400.
       With filters the backlog is filtered before it is cut; "*" keeps up to 160. hello echoes the filter.
  GET /live/more?id=N         the full filtered text of event N (the stream cuts texts at 2 KB), JSON
  GET /live/health             JSON status, no content
  GET /live/agents             SSE for the dashboard's Agents tab: "hello", then "agents" {now, hours, main, agents[]}
                               (lib/agentfeed.py snapshot: running / stalled agents + those ended in the last 6 h, the
                               Main row) whenever it changes, checked every 2 s; ": ping" every 15 s. Up to 6 viewers.
  GET /live/agent?id=ID|main   SSE: one agent's (or the main session's) activity: "hello", "steps" [backlog, results
                               folded in], then live "step" events {s, t, k: start|in|tool|res|say|end, n, d, ok, ref,
                               x, len}; "gone" when the main session rotated (the page reconnects). Up to 8 viewers.
                               Strictly filtered (agentfeed.clean, fail closed): tool names, the agent's own short
                               descriptions, ok/error, its prose lines; never inputs, outputs, prompts, the result.
  GET /live/ci                 SSE for the Health and CI tabs: "hello", then "ci" (lib/cifeed.py snapshot: land queue,
                               last 15 lands, nightly, hub runner, headline, legacy suites, deploys; branch/step/suite
                               names, releases, times, counts only)
                               whenever it changes, checked every 2 s; ": ping" every 15 s. Up to 6 viewers.
Event: {id, t, edge, from, to, kind, chip, actor, text?, more?, meta{exit, ms, bytes, cmd, desc, hidden, redacted}}

Privacy (tests: ~/opt/flowd-tests/run.sh)
  * Strict allowlist: text only for known tools and message kinds; an unknown tool, or a result whose call was not
    seen, is metadata only.
  * Vault (all data that I can see, not just metadata): a command or path touching
    vault/tgread/paperless/context/signals/bills/contracts/firefly/gmail/recall/deadlines/gift-radar/missing-docs or my
    transcripts (VAULT_RE) goes to edge me→vault WITH its content, like every other tool: the command I run and the
    full output my session receives (answers, flags, cards, digests). Subagent results and every inbox note are shown
    too; nothing is masked. What happens inside the vault (Telegram/Gmail/paperless/Firefly -> policy filter -> local
    LLM) never reaches my session, so flowd has no edge for it and cannot show it.
  * Secrets: outputs of commands/reads touching ~/.secrets, .env, credentials, ssh keys, htpasswd, basic-auth or card
    files are never shown; every text goes through secretscan.redact and must then pass secretscan.scan, else it is
    dropped; without secretscan no text is sent at all (fail closed).
"""
